ng change you've seen  in yourself or in your own relationships  or in your professional life  that you didn't expect but came from  this so i like to say that as human  beings  we tend to fluctuate between two modes  of thinking that are  inaccurate so we tend to think that we  are either omnipotent  everything is in our control or some  aspect of something is in our control  or we tend to think that we're impotent  we have absolutely no control  over anything and i was in a  relationship  last year where i was basically acting  impotent i was acting as if i was  completely powerless  um i was also acting as if the guy had  and he does um had infinite potential  and he does um  because everyone has infinite potential  but at the same time like  we just were not on the same energy  levels  um and i i had this it was drawn  out for far longer than it should have  been and i should have basically  split the difference between impotence  and omnipotence and say okay you don't  have all the power in the world but you  do have some power  in this situation so let's start leaning  into that power  and that's something that i learned  through  practicing theory of enchantment through  teaching theory of enchantment through  seeing how other people  respond to theory of enchantment and  that's that's something that i had to  i had to learn because part of me  struggles from the fact that just  because someone has  unlimited potential and they do doesn't  mean that i have to be the one  to be present and wait for it to  come to fruition and it might not come  to fruition that's the whole point of  potential right  so i had to learn that potential doesn't  mean  guarantee um but you still have  power to do things and to change the  situation if you want to  so that's something i had to learn in  the i did learn in the past year  i guess i have one more one more which  was  what set you on this journey in the  first place what happened  that you went this can't be right  this 